<mxfile host="65bd71144e">
    <diagram id="mindmap" name="Overview">
        <mxGraphModel dx="1227" dy="977" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="0" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1240" pageHeight="980" math="1" shadow="0">
            <root>
                <mxCell id="0"/>
                <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
                <mxCell id="hcmm" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Constrained Mixture Model&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Humprhey Rajagopal 2002&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="60" width="210" x="10" y="12.5" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="hom" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="&lt;b&gt;The idea of constrained mixture theroy is that a material consisting of multiple constituents deforms with one global defromation gradient \(\mathbf F\), this means interconstituent interactions are simplified&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="85" width="420" x="10" y="80" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="wBruslNdQrpOLpaYggGj-1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Homogenized CMM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;(Cyron et al. 2016)" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="60" width="210" x="10" y="620" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="wBruslNdQrpOLpaYggGj-2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="&lt;b&gt;In classical CMM every constituent has a history of mass depositions at certain current deformation gradients \(\mathbf F(\tau)\), which degrade over time. Therefor a heridatry integral of over all simulation steps has to be built for every step&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="85" width="420" x="10" y="165" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;Mass deposited at time \(\tau\)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;\(\mathbf F_e^j(s,\tau) = \mathbf F(s)\,\mathbf F^{-1}(\tau)\,\mathbf G^j\)&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;diagram: page Constrained mixture&lt;/i&gt;" id="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-2">
                    <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;" vertex="1">
                        <mxGeometry height="80" width="400" x="470" y="250" as="geometry"/>
                    </mxCell>
                </UserObject>
                <mxCell id="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-5" edge="1" parent="1" source="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-4" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;" target="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-2">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-4" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="&lt;b&gt;Similar to Kinematic Growth theory the deformation gradient can be split into elastic \(\mathbf F_e^j\) and non elastic part \(\mathbf F(\tau)\), \(\mathbf G^j(\tau)\), where \(\mathbf F(\tau)\) describes the deformation at deposition time of the cohort and \(\mathbf G^j\) the prestretch of a certain constituent&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="85" width="420" x="10" y="250" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-6" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="&lt;b&gt;Mass is constantly added \(m^j(s)\) and removed \(q^j(s,\tau)\) depending on various factors, even if mass is constant due to removal and generating being equal, new deposited mass may is added with a certain prestretch \(\mathbf G^j\) that might be different from the removed mass current stress, therefor causing a change in overall stress, which is called remodeling&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="85" width="420" x="10" y="335" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-10" edge="1" parent="1" source="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-8" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-9">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-8" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="&lt;b&gt;The helmholtz energy of the material at a certain time step is calculated with an integral over time of the exisiting mass at a certain time point where each time point has a different elastic and inelastic deformation&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="85" width="420" x="10" y="505" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <UserObject label="\(\Psi^j(s) = \Psi_0^j(s) + \int_0^s \frac{m^j(\tau)}{\rho}\,q^j(s,\tau)\,\hat W^j\big(\mathbf F_e^j(s,\tau)\big)\,d\tau\)" id="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-9">
                    <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;" vertex="1">
                        <mxGeometry height="80" width="400" x="470" y="505" as="geometry"/>
                    </mxCell>
                </UserObject>
                <mxCell id="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-11" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="&lt;b&gt;Net increase of mass, called growth causes volumetric growth, therefor also changes the stress state. This is represented as \(\mathbf F_g^j\), in the classical theory this is set to \(\mathbf I\), therefor no cohort changes its stress-free state, the volume follows from the mass via \(J\) and the shape from equilibrium and turnover&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="85" width="420" x="10" y="420" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-14" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f2f8f0;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;" value="We need to track the deposition and degredation of each mass at a certain current deformation \(\mathbf F(\tau)\)" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="70" width="280" x="900" y="140" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-15" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f2f8f0;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;" value="The tracked variables are:&lt;br&gt;\(\mathbf F(\tau)\)&lt;br&gt;and for each constituent:&lt;br&gt;\(m^j(\tau),\; q^j(s,\tau)\)&lt;br&gt;in case of growth being stress dependent&lt;br&gt;\(\boldsymbol\sigma^j(\tau)\),&lt;br&gt;in case of changing deposition prestretch or fiber direction&lt;br&gt;\(\mathbf G^j(\tau),\; \mathbf a^j(\tau)\)" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="160" width="280" x="900" y="210" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="f_hom" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;" value="\(\mathbf x^j(\mathbf X,s) = \mathbf x(\mathbf X,s)\;\;\forall j \;\Rightarrow\; \mathbf F^j = \mathbf F\)&lt;br&gt;\(\boldsymbol\sigma = \sum_j \boldsymbol\sigma^j\)" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="80" width="400" x="470" y="82.5" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e_hom" edge="1" parent="1" source="hom" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;" target="f_hom">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="f_her" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;" value="\(\rho^j(s) = \rho^j_0(s) + \int_0^s m^j(\tau)\,q^j(s,\tau)\,d\tau\)" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="80" width="400" x="470" y="332.5" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e_her" edge="1" parent="1" source="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-6" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" target="f_her">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e_grow" edge="1" parent="1" source="0QsqrzKswuEvI0QZ2M8a-11" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;" target="PrEDxpIs1w5A9Yhl0JyS-2">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="PrEDxpIs1w5A9Yhl0JyS-1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;" value="\(\rho_{tot}(s) = \sum_j \rho^j(s)\)&lt;br&gt;\(J = \det\mathbf F = \rho_{tot}(s)/\rho_{tot}(0)\) (constant density)" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="80" width="400" x="470" y="165" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;Generalized law for per constituent growth&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;\(\mathbf F_e^j(s,\tau) = \mathbf F(s)\,\big[\mathbf F_g^j(s)\big]^{-1}\,\Big[\mathbf F(\tau)\,\big[\mathbf F_g^j(\tau)\big]^{-1}\Big]^{-1}\,\mathbf G^j\)&lt;br&gt;classical: \(\mathbf F_g^j = \mathbf I\), Braeu / Maes: \(\mathbf F_g^j = \mathbf F_g\)" id="PrEDxpIs1w5A9Yhl0JyS-2">
                    <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;" vertex="1">
                        <mxGeometry height="80" width="400" x="470" y="419" as="geometry"/>
                    </mxCell>
                </UserObject>
                <mxCell id="PrEDxpIs1w5A9Yhl0JyS-3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="&lt;b&gt;The idea of the temporal homogenized CMM is that we represent the hereditary integral over time with a representative growth deformation \(\mathbf F_g\) and a remodeling deformation \(\mathbf F_r^j\) per constituent&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="85" width="420" x="10" y="680" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="sROYP4MHdx0KK_W_iqqb-1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="&lt;b&gt;We can do this by assuming a stress rate caused by remodeling \(\dot{\boldsymbol\sigma}_r^j\), due to material at a certain stretch degrading and new material being deposited at a certain prestretch (mass average over the cohorts, one explicit Euler step)&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="85" width="420" x="10" y="765" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <UserObject label="\(\dot{\boldsymbol\sigma}^j_r(s) = -\frac{\dot\varrho^j_{0+}(s)}{\varrho^j_0(s)}\left[\boldsymbol\sigma^j(s)-\boldsymbol\sigma^j_{pre}(s)\right]\)&lt;br&gt;\(\boldsymbol\sigma^j_{pre}(s) = \mathbf R(s)\,\boldsymbol\sigma^j_h\,\mathbf R^T(s)\)" id="sROYP4MHdx0KK_W_iqqb-2">
                    <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;" vertex="1">
                        <mxGeometry height="85" width="460" x="470" y="765" as="geometry"/>
                    </mxCell>
                </UserObject>
                <mxCell id="sROYP4MHdx0KK_W_iqqb-3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="&lt;b&gt;We can now set this equal to the change of stress due to the elastic deformation gradient changing, where we keep the deformation and growth gradient constant as they are assigned by the outward solver&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="85" width="420" x="10" y="850" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <UserObject label="\(\dot{\boldsymbol\sigma}^j_r = \left[\frac{\partial\boldsymbol\sigma^j}{\partial\mathbf F^j_e}:\dot{\mathbf F}^j_e\right]_{\mathbf F,\,\mathbf F^j_g=\mathrm{const}}\) \(= -\left[\frac{\partial\boldsymbol\sigma^j}{\partial\mathbf F^j_e}\right]_{\mathbf F,\,\mathbf F^j_g=\mathrm{const}}:\left[\mathbf F^j_e\,\dot{\mathbf F}^j_r\left(\mathbf F^j_r\right)^{-1}\right]\)&lt;br&gt;\(= -\left[\frac{\partial\boldsymbol\sigma^j}{\partial\mathbf F^j_e}\right]_{\mathbf F,\,\mathbf F^j_g=\mathrm{const}}:\left[\mathbf F^j_e\,\mathbf L^j_r\right],\quad \mathbf L^j_r = \dot{\mathbf F}^j_r\left(\mathbf F^j_r\right)^{-1}\)" id="sROYP4MHdx0KK_W_iqqb-4">
                    <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;" vertex="1">
                        <mxGeometry height="85" width="460" x="470" y="850" as="geometry"/>
                    </mxCell>
                </UserObject>
                <mxCell id="f_hcmm_kin" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;arcSize=20;" value="\(\mathbf F^j_e(s) = \mathbf F(s)\left[\mathbf F^j_g(s)\right]^{-1}\left[\mathbf F^j_r(s)\right]^{-1}\)&lt;br&gt;\(\dot\varrho^j_0(s) = \dot\varrho^j_{0+}(s)+\dot\varrho^j_{0-}(s)\)&lt;br&gt;Cyron / Braeu: \(\mathbf F^j_g = \mathbf F_g\) for all \(j\)" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="85" width="460" x="470" y="680" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e_f_hcmm_kin" edge="1" parent="1" source="PrEDxpIs1w5A9Yhl0JyS-3" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;" target="f_hcmm_kin">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e_sROYP4MHdx0KK_W_iqqb-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="sROYP4MHdx0KK_W_iqqb-1" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;" target="sROYP4MHdx0KK_W_iqqb-2">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="e_sROYP4MHdx0KK_W_iqqb-4" edge="1" parent="1" source="sROYP4MHdx0KK_W_iqqb-3" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;" target="sROYP4MHdx0KK_W_iqqb-4">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>